== listing shape == (1389 files swept, 2 allowlisted)
  [allowed] probes/lib/latch_check.py:96: 2-line listing (5565467e6422) — C-BIOS, same window and same adjudication as the omsx_repl.py entry below: the two comment lines restate the chget_char boundaries this checker scores (D-LATCH2, docs/spec-probe-latch2.md). Surfaced only after knife K1b forced the comment leaders `; # //` into the prefix class — under the first cut this file was invisible, which is the whole reason that fix landed.
  [allowed] probes/lib/omsx_repl.py:379: 3-line listing (edb676f694b2) — C-BIOS, not a proprietary reference ROM: allowed-sources.md grades C-BIOS source B/Conditional — a peer clean-room reimplementation under BSD-2 whose source this project already patches (cbios-repack/), and NOT the reference implementation zerobas reimplements. The run is 3 instructions of the keyboard-buffer path, in a docstring explaining the D-LATCH2 injection window (docs/spec-probe-latch2.md §5.5); the same docstring is explicit about the line it stays on ("locating chget in the reference needs a disassembly this project does not do"). Probe source, not shipped ROM source. Flagged for the human paper trail 2026-08-06 (D-DOCJUDGE §2.6) — a judgement docs/clean-room-audit.md reserves for a human, which is why it is written down here rather than decided by the tool.
  clean — no unallowlisted decoded-instruction listings

== hex-dump rows == (1389 files swept, 1 allowlisted)
  [allowed] tools/audit_citations.py:428: hex-dump row (0c30593198a1) — The check's own synthetic self-test vector (_DUMP_VEC). INVENTED bytes — no provenance, no derivation, not decoded from anything — so recording it forbids nothing; a REAL positive vector would be the artifact this check refuses and would make the tool its own first finding. Unlike check 5's LISTING_LINE this rule is not anchored at line start (a dump lives inside a markdown table cell), so the vector is necessarily a hit on this file. That is turned into the canary rather than worked around: if this line stops matching, check 6 has gone blind and exits 2 rather than printing "clean".
  clean — no unallowlisted hex-dump rows  (narrow by design: this is the dump ROW only, not the raw-byte class — docs/spec-audit-citations-bytes.md §3.1)

